---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/alternatives";
const title = "Shopify marketing alternatives: choose the job to replace";
const desc = "Route a capture, email, SMS or event-ownership problem to the right replacement investigation, then prove the handover on controlled records.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <p class="badge">Replacement planning · November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <article class="container prose-shopify pb-16">
    <h2>Name the broken job before choosing a replacement</h2>
    <p>Start with a failure you can reproduce: a capture field lost at sync, a purchase arriving after a cart reminder, a bill driven by inactive profiles, or an unowned reply queue. Repairing a working incumbent can preserve templates, consent history and trained operators. Replacing it can remove duplicate work or supply a missing capability, provided the new owner can demonstrate that job. This directory routes an investigation; it does not rank vendors or claim that every listed tool sends SMS.</p>
    <h2>Replacement, comparison or a sending-layer repair?</h2>
    <p>Use an app-specific replacement page when you already know what you are leaving. Use <a class="link" href="/compare">head-to-head comparisons</a> when two candidates must answer the same brief, including <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-omnisend">Klaviyo versus Omnisend</a>. Use the <a class="link" href="/apps">app directory</a> for initial capability research. A failed welcome after a successful quiz may require repairing the destination sender rather than replacing capture. Adding another sender without resolving queue ownership can multiply the failure.</p>
    <h2>Route by the operating job</h2>
    <table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Job under review</th><th>Investigation path</th><th>Evidence needed</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>SMS dispatch and replies</td><td><a href="/apps/postscript">Postscript</a> or <a href="/apps/attentive">Attentive</a></td><td>Destination coverage, sender access, opt-out propagation, reply staffing and delivered-segment charges.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Cross-channel event ownership</td><td><a href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo</a>, Omnisend or Sendlane research</td><td>One order ID must cancel the relevant queued reminder; decide who owns email and SMS collisions.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Capture, quiz and identity handoff</td><td><a href="/alternatives/justuno-alternative">Replacing Justuno</a>; inspect Privy as a capture candidate</td><td>Compare required fields, targeting and supported installation before considering downstream sends.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Email education beside an existing text sender</td><td><a href="/apps/sequenzy">Sequenzy email review</a> or an existing email platform</td><td>Template and event fit, maintainable consent boundaries, and the added integration cost; no default second platform.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Native or simpler messaging</td><td>Shopify Messaging and Shopify Email official resources below</td><td>Current eligibility, actual channel scope and the events needed; a simpler editor is useful only if the journey remains operable.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Replenishment or stock timing</td><td><a href="/use-cases">Use-case playbooks</a></td><td>Stock expiry, subscription state, purchase exits and support ownership before the tool decision.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <h2>App-specific exit notes</h2>
