    <h2>Permission and purchase exits come before dispatch</h2>
    <p>Preserve the source, timestamp, disclosure version and channel-specific subscription and suppression history. Unknown permission is not permission. The receiving sender must enforce current eligibility and applicable destination/timezone rules at dispatch, including opt-outs received after import. A purchase should cancel the matching recovery job without silently canceling every unrelated service message. Assign an owner to unresolved identities and contradictory records. Review <a class="link" href="/guides/consent">consent</a>, <a class="link" href="/guides/tcpa">compliance questions</a>, <a class="link" href="/guides/quiet-hours">quiet hours</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/deliverability">deliverability</a> for the implementation brief.</p>
    <h2>Compare economics on the same workload</h2>
    <p>Request the same normal and peak-month audience, message mix, destinations, encoding, support and contract assumptions from each candidate. Include billable suppressed profiles, segments and carrier charges, middleware, migration labor and retained subscriptions. Compare incremental contribution against a suitable holdout after merchandise costs, incentives, refunds, messaging and support; count a discount once. Platform-attributed revenue alone is not incremental lift. The <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">pricing worksheet</a> helps expose a cheap base plan with expensive handoffs.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance and rollback gates</h2>
    <p>Inventory flows, sender identities, links, templates, events and waiting people first. On controlled records, demonstrate capture to destination, one welcome, a retried event without duplicate dispatch, purchase-before-send cancellation, opt-out-before-send suppression and a visible failed delivery queue. Keep IDs, timestamps and expected versus actual states. These are proposed exercises, not tests performed for this directory. Set the observation window to the journey and billing cycle rather than an arbitrary migration deadline. Release a bounded cohort only when the named operator can pause it; keep one live owner per job, preserve a rollback export, and reconcile waiting people before either system resumes.</p>
    <h2>The campaign calendar remains an operating responsibility</h2>
    <p>A new app does not decide how many offers a subscriber should receive. Keep a shared calendar, offer eligibility, stock truth and stop thresholds across channels. Preserve meaningful VIP access without requiring a discount, and isolate an incentive experiment from routine full-price communication. See <a class="link" href="/guides/campaign-restraint">campaign restraint</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/offer-discipline">offer discipline</a>. Choose the smallest change that resolves the documented job with a supportable owner.</p>

